    "draft-ietf-httpbis-layered-cookies"
  ],
  "location": "Fetch, determine the same-site mode, steps 4 to 6",
  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Fetch: cross-site subresources and redirected POST requests get the highest same-site mode",
      "summary": "No step compares a request with its client. The ancestor check looks at parents only, so a first request from a top-level page on a to b reaches the last step. The redirect check skips a hop when the origin of the request is same site with the URL before it, so a form POST from a to a that redirects to b reaches the last step too.",
      "impact": "An image, frame or credentialed fetch from a top-level page on a to b: by the text SameSite=Strict and SameSite=Lax cookies are sent; Chromium 156 and Firefox 157 do not send them. A top-level form POST from a to a with a 307 to b: by the text they are sent; Chromium 156, Firefox 157 and WebKit 27.2 do not send them. Existing web-platform-tests in cookies/samesite expect the browser result.",
      "correction": "Compare the request with its client for non-navigation requests, and count every hop of the URL list."
    }
  },
